WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:07.067
After preparing the white-ink artwork, open DTG Placement to
position the actual output on a selected

2
00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:07.548
platen.

3
00:00:09.053 --> 00:00:11.688
First set the platen width and height.

4
00:00:11.688 --> 00:00:16.542
Placement uses real dimensions and preserves
the artwork's print size.

5
00:00:18.487 --> 00:00:23.263
Drag the artwork in the left preview and the
position values update with it.

6
00:00:23.263 --> 00:00:28.039
You can also enter horizontal and vertical
positions for precise adjustment.

7
00:00:29.653 --> 00:00:32.521
Center guides help confirm alignment.

8
00:00:32.521 --> 00:00:37.637
Arrow keys allow fine adjustments, while
Shift uses a larger step.

9
00:00:39.387 --> 00:00:43.620
Once the position is confirmed, export
the placement TIFF.

10
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:51.064
The software saves color artwork and W1 on the actual platen
canvas, together with a placement record.

11
00:00:51.387 --> 00:00:54.440
Inspect color and white ink in the actual output.

12
00:00:54.440 --> 00:01:00.609
The platen and garment illustrations are alignment
references and are not printed into the artwork.

13
00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:08.833
From white-ink control to platen placement, the workflow
keeps processing, positioning, and output

14
00:01:08.833 --> 00:01:10.221
inspection connected.
